      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Row 101, Japanese shield fern (autumn fern), the hardy outdoor fern of the 'hardy ferns' row; not the houseplant ferns of rows 28 and 36. Three care sources agree on shade to part shade, moist humusy soil and a slow, semi-evergreen clump. Light conflict: RHS also allows full sun with plenty of water; the shade reading of NC State and Missouri BG is kept. Drought conflict: NC State and RHS say brief drought or dry shade is tolerated, Missouri BG says the soil must not dry out; the conservative reading (no tolerance) is kept. Size: RHS 0.5 to 1 m, NC State 1.5 to 2 ft by 2 to 3 ft, Missouri BG 1.5 to 2.5 ft; 75 by 90 cm is the agent's mapping. Hardiness H4 is the RHS rating (NC State zones 6b to 12, Missouri BG 5 to 8). Dormancy none: semi-evergreen. NC State warns it may naturalise and turn invasive in the US south-east. Toxicity: no source states any, so people and pets stay unknown. Es and it names are machine drafts."
      },
